title: 'Zhang et al., "Agentic Context Engineering" (ACE, ICLR 2026): an LLM rewriting a context whole collapsed it, from 18,282 tokens to 122 and below the accuracy of no context at all; small itemized changes, merged by plain code, avoided it.'
pid: 57c1bda1-1a18-4fb1-bf79-42fff93c8be0
body: |2-
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04618
  Read. Accuracy fell from 66.7 to 57.1, against 63.7 with no
  adaptation. Items carry counts of how often each was helpful or
  harmful; duplicates are pruned by embedding similarity. Without
  ground-truth labels or an execution signal, "both ACE and DC may
  degrade in performance" (one online run lost 3.4 points). Took: move
  and add, do not rewrite whole; and reflection with nothing outside to
  check against can make memory worse.
